      "originalText": "COMPOSITION / INHERITANCE & TRADE-OFFS\nClients use the Logger object; they neither inherit from it nor own separate logger objects. That is shared access, not a “has-a” composition relationship.\nGood for a truly shared resource; trade-off: global access can hide dependencies and make tests harder. Prefer injected dependencies when one shared instance is not a real requirement.\nThread safety note: C++11+ safely initializes this local static once. That does not automatically make mutable Logger operations or their shared state thread-safe.",
